What is `Order["shipping"]["zip"]`?

```ts
interface Order {
  shipping: { city: string; zip?: number };
}
```

What is `keyof Dict`?

```ts
interface Dict {
  [key: string]: number;
}
```

A developer makes a typo in the key. What does the compiler do?

```ts
interface User { id: number; name: string }
type A = Omit<User, "nmae">;
type B = Pick<User, "nmae">;
```

Type the union that `Item` resolves to (any order).

```ts
const arr = [1, "a", true];
type Item = (typeof arr)[number];
```

What are `keyof (A | B)` and `keyof (A & B)`?

```ts
type A = { a: 1; c: 3 };
type B = { b: 2; c: 3 };
```

A team removes `id` from a discriminated union and then cannot read `radius` anymore. Which explanation and fix are correct?

```ts
type Circle = { kind: "circle"; id: string; radius: number };
type Square = { kind: "square"; id: string; side: number };
type NoId = Omit<Circle | Square, "id">;
```

What does `OnlyStrings<{ a: string; b: number; c: "x" }>` resolve to?

```ts
type OnlyStrings<T> = {
  [K in keyof T as T[K] extends string ? K : never]: T[K];
};
```

Why does this getters type need `string & K` instead of plain `K`?

```ts
type Getters<T> = {
  [K in keyof T as `get${Capitalize<string & K>}`]: () => T[K];
};
```

Given these overloads, which two statements are true? (Choose two.)

```ts
function parse(x: string): number;
function parse(x: number): string;
function parse(x: any): any { return x; }
```

What is the type of `c.length`?

```ts
type C = { [K in keyof [number, string]]: boolean };
declare const c: C;
```

What is `Omit<Props, "id">["name"]`?

```ts
interface Props {
  [key: string]: unknown;
  id: number;
  name: string;
}
```

What is `Mark<A | B>`?

```ts
type A = { a: 1; c: 3 };
type B = { b: 2; c: 3 };
type Mark<T> = { [K in keyof T]: true };
```
